WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
In September 1996, in the&nbsp;
town of Woodsboro, California,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:06.720
two high school students went on a crime&nbsp;
spree that resulted in the loss of five lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.040
while dressed up in these “Father Death” Halloween&nbsp;
costumes. One of the assailants, Billy Loomis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.720
was motivated to get revenge on his classmate,&nbsp;
Sidney Prescott, because Sidney’s mother had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:19.040
participated in an affair with Billy’s father,&nbsp;
resulting in his mother abandoning the family.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.000
Sidney eventually defeated Billy&nbsp;
and his accomplice, Stu Macher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.680
with the help of on-the-scene reporter Gale&nbsp;
Weathers. Gale went on to write a bestselling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.080
novel about the incident called The Woodsboro&nbsp;
Murders. The book was a follow up to her 1995&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.720
book Wrongfully Accused:&nbsp;
The Maureen Prescott Murder.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.600
According to Gale Weathers.com, The Woodsboro&nbsp;
Murders came out in late 1996. “Gale Weathers'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.840
second novel details the murderous plot of two&nbsp;
angry teenagers determined to murder Sidney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.400
Prescott and her innocent friends. In a bizarre&nbsp;
turn of events, the author herself became not only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.440
a target of the killers, but a hero. Ms. Weathers'&nbsp;
book became the Sunrise Studios hit movie: Stab.”

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.760
Stab would go on to become one of the all time&nbsp;
great long running horror movie franchises. To&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.240
learn about the often unknown details of Stab&nbsp;
movies, including the lost trailer for Stab 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.640
the differences only included in the theatrical cut of the original Stab, and the dirty movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.280
studio secrets detailed on this anonymous&nbsp;
website, stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.308
This video is sponsored by Audible.

00:01:11.517 --> 00:01:15.235
(metal music)

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.600
Welcome to Horror History. The rights to produce&nbsp;
the movie adaptation of The Woodsboro Murders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.520
were granted to Sunrise Studios, who came to&nbsp;
the famed horror movie producer John Milton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.720
the man responsible for movies like Frankenpimp,&nbsp;
Is Somebody There? and The 1st House on the Right.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:35.120
He also produced Amazombies, Space Psycho&nbsp;
and Creature From The San Andreas Fault,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.680
all movies that featured actress Rena Reynolds,&nbsp;
which coincidentally, was a stage name for Maureen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.000
Roberts. She ended up getting knocked up at one&nbsp;
of John Milton’s parties; it is unlikely that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.560
conception was consensual though. After giving&nbsp;
birth to a son, named Roman, she abandoned him and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.720
left Hollywood to reside in Woodsboro, where she&nbsp;
was killed by Billy Loomis to set the real-life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:57.200
events that Stab was based on into motion.&nbsp;
Milton recognized that Maureen, who had married&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.840
and become Maureen Prescott, was Rena, from his&nbsp;
movies, but decided to keep that fact to himself.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.880
– I couldn’t tell anyone.&nbsp;
Can you imagine the press?

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:09.760
– But even before that, Sunrise Studios had another&nbsp;
Woodsboro connection, so to learn about that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.560
let’s take it back to 1972, when Billy&nbsp;
Loomis’s father lived in Los Angeles.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.920
(mysterious music)

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.360
In the early 70s, Henry Loomis was a&nbsp;
lawyer who worked for Sunrise Studios,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.280
and his services were required thanks to a pair&nbsp;
of incidents that occured. The first was on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:32.080
production of the cheerleader slasher movie, Is&nbsp;
Somebody There? Actress Elaine Varsi went missing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.520
prompting Mr. Loomis to send a memo out to&nbsp;
the company, telling them not to make any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.960
comment on the case. Just months later, on June&nbsp;
13th, 1972, during the production of a Russian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.280
terrorist thriller called Shutout! an actress&nbsp;
named Loretta Fisher reportedly disappeared from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.280
the movie’s set in the middle of shooting one of&nbsp;
her scenes, which left everyone baffled.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.240
Ms. Fisher’s family eventually&nbsp;
came after Sunrise Studios for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.240
damages. This lawsuit went on for&nbsp;
over 2 years, but on April 22nd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:01.280
1974, either Mr. Loomis was able to find a legal&nbsp;
loophole of some kind that voided the lawsuit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.880
or Ms. Fisher’s family just had no&nbsp;
money to pursue further litigation.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.040
According to the anonymous expose website&nbsp;
Sunrise Sucks, “the Sunrise lawyer Henry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.680
Loomis parted ways with the Studio the very next&nbsp;
day after the case was closed. Rumor has it he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:18.640
left Hollywood for good and set up his own private&nbsp;
practice in a small Midwestern town: Woodsboro.”

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.920
Of course, we now know that one part&nbsp;
isn’t accurate, because Woodsboro is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.520
located in Northern California, not&nbsp;
the Midwest. Some time after this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.560
Henry would meet and marry a woman&nbsp;
named Debbie, and together they gave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:32.960
birth to a son named Billy in the late 70s,&nbsp;
before his affair with Maureen Prescott.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.720
I include this story, because the fact&nbsp;
that Henry and Maureen both worked at,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.280
had a controversy at, and left Sunrise Studios&nbsp;
before having their affair in Woodsboro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.560
which was instrumental in knocking over&nbsp;
the dominoes that led to the creation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:48.480
of the Stab franchise, all seems like&nbsp;
it’s too convenient to be coincidental.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:52.960
But that being said, I can’t picture any&nbsp;
scenario where it isn’t coincidental.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.640
It’s not like John Milton told them to go to&nbsp;
have an affair in Woodsboro so that he could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.440
one day make a movie about it. And Maureen’s son&nbsp;
Roman was only a baby when she left Hollywood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.440
so he couldn’t have played a hand in it either.&nbsp;
So I think the takeaway here is that Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:09.840
corrupted both Maureen and Henry. There were&nbsp;
shady things going on all the time at Sunrise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:13.680
and the bad behavior rubbed off on the&nbsp;
two of them. They became shady themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.000
which led to them having an affair. Sunrise&nbsp;
Studios was not the mastermind behind Stab’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.360
true story, but they still did&nbsp;
kind of cause it, indirectly.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:25.040
As I mentioned, Billy and Stu slashed up their&nbsp;
high school and Gale wrote a book about it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.520
which became Stab. Robert Rodriguez, fresh&nbsp;
off the heels of From Dusk Till Dawn, was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:33.120
brought on to direct. Will Kennison&nbsp;
adapted Gale’s book into the screenplay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.200
and Dante Paltrow composed the score.&nbsp;
Cinematography was done by Hawken Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.680
who had worked with Milton on Frankenpimp,&nbsp;
and the movie was filmed in Stab-O-Vision!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.840
I don’t know what that is, but I assume it’s&nbsp;
some kind of blacklight effect that shows certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.400
secrets when viewed through a special lens,&nbsp;
such as a specially outfitted Ghostface mask.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.000
Tori Spelling, who had played Donna&nbsp;
Martin in Beverly Hills 90210,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.560
was cast to play Sidney Prescott. David Schwimmer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.080
of F•R•I•E•N•D•S fame was cast as the&nbsp;
inexperienced Deputy Dewey Riley. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:04.880
got Luke Wilson to play Billy Loomis and Heather&nbsp;
Graham played the human knife-block Casey Becker.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:09.280
Quick note here from me. After this, the&nbsp;
cast listed on the Sunrise Studios website&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.360
that promoted Scream 3 does not line up with&nbsp;
the cast listed in the search results shown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:18.880
in Scream (2022). I’m considering Scream (2022) to&nbsp;
be canon, so I’ll be using the names listed there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.320
Does this mean that nothing from&nbsp;
the promotional websites is canon?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:26.240
Yes, probably. But I still included the stuff&nbsp;
that doesn’t directly contradict the movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:29.760
because it makes this video way&nbsp;
more fun. Back to the cast list.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:34.960
Jennifer Jolie played Gale Weathers. Christopher&nbsp;
Speed (also known as Joe Blo Nobody) played movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:39.280
buff Randy Meeks, and Alicia Silverstone&nbsp;
played Sidney’s best friend, Tatum Riley.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:44.000
A young Vince Vaughn was cast in his first major&nbsp;
role to play Stu Macher. Ron Howard made a cameo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.080
as Principal Himbry. Craig Bierko, coming&nbsp;
off his success in The Long Kiss Goodnight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.200
played the role of Cotton Weary, the&nbsp;
man being framed for Maureen’s murder.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.120
The film opens with Casey Becker receiving a&nbsp;
mysterious call before getting in the shower.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.160
Her masked stalker chases her through&nbsp;
the house, and out to the pool area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:00.560
where she’s tackled and gutted by Ghostface.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.600
Sidney Prescott and her friends hear&nbsp;
about the murders at school the next day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.040
and in the evening, Sidney has her own&nbsp;
encounter with Ghostface, which she believes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:11.520
to be her boyfriend, Billy Loomis. However, she&nbsp;
receives another creepy phone call after this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:16.160
while Billy is in custody, so Billy is let go.&nbsp;
He runs into Sidney at school the next day.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.800
– They let me go Sid, I&nbsp;
didn’t do it.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:22.880
He’s lying. He tries to convince Sidney to get&nbsp;
over her Mom’s death so they can be intimate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:27.360
again, which doesn’t go well. Sidney manages to&nbsp;
escape Ghostface once more in the school bathroom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.440
and this time classes are canceled. Shortly&nbsp;
after, so is the school principal’s life.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.520
Tatum’s boyfriend Stu Macher hosts a party that&nbsp;
evening, where Randy explains that horror movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:39.280
tend to abide by a set of rules, which the&nbsp;
killers in Woodsboro seem to be following.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:45.280
– [Randy (Stab)] Never ever ever, under any circumstances, say,&nbsp;
‘I’ll be right back. Cause you won’t be back.’

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:49.920
This results in the deaths of Tatum, the news&nbsp;
station cameraman Kenny, and almost Randy himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:54.560
but in the end, Sidney and Gale are able to defeat&nbsp;
Billy and Stu before any more lives are lost.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.520
The studio would go all out to&nbsp;
promote the release of Stab,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:01.840
but at the premiere, things&nbsp;
would get a little bit messy.

